      "writtenOn": "2025-11-07T19:25:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `pdc_power_mgmt_set_current_limit()` ensures that the Rp value and SRC PDO values are in sync.\n\nBut we probably don\u0027t want to wait to send new source caps.  If we\u0027re currently a SRC, the state machine will have to process all the sub-states of `pdc_src_attached_run` before it updates the source caps.\n\nYou could add a new enum to `enum attached_state_t` so that we don\u0027t set redundant policy flags.\n\n```\nenum attached_state_t {\n    INIT_STATE,\n    UNATTACHED_STATE,\n\n...\n\nThen you can call `pdc_power_mgmt_set_current_limit()` and it won\u0027t set any policy flags and you can still send SRC CAPS inline here.",
